0	192	Glenn Micallef (Maltese pronunciation: [ˈɡlɛnː mɪˈkɐlːɛf]; born 30 July 1989) is a Maltese civil servant who was Chief of Staff to the Prime Minister of Malta, Robert Abela, from 2020 to 2024.
193	312	Since December 2024 he has served as European Commissioner for Intergenerational Fairness, Youth, Culture and Sport.



312	459	Early life
Micallef graduated from the University of Malta with a bachelor's degree in commerce and economics and a Masters degree in European law.
460	517	As a student, he served as president of Pulse in 2010.



517	645	Career
He later worked at the foreign affairs ministry, where he was head of the EU Coordination Department and the Brexit Unit.
646	741	In January 2020, Micallef was named European affairs advisor to Prime Minister Robert Abela.



